--- CONTROL NEEDLE (§11.4.201(7)(b)) ---
A zero from a hand-written query is not evidence until the query is shown
able to return non-zero through the SAME path. Two items closed TODAY via
the 'close' subcommand, which requires --evidence:
BOB-092|Fixed|1|docs/qa/BOB-092/closure_run_20260821.log
BOB-136|Fixed|1|docs/qa/BOB-136/closure-evidence.md

NEEDLE VERDICT: PASS — the query returns 1 evidence row each for the two
properly-closed items. The ten zeros above are real ABSENCE, not a blind query.

=== WHAT THIS MEANS FOR ACCEPTANCE (c) ===
Not one of the ten has ANY recorded evidence_path. This is the discriminator
predicted by BOB-166's root cause: 'close' migrates AND records evidence;
'update --status' does neither. All ten bear the signature of the second path.

So draining them is NOT a mechanical migration. Each row needs its evidence
LOCATED (it may exist under docs/qa/<id>/ without ever being recorded) or
PRODUCED, and any row whose closure cannot be evidenced must be honestly
REOPENED rather than migrated on a bare assertion (§11.4.226: a status must
not outrun its evidence).

